of exposure in erg/cm2 required to produce specified density) as printed; r = cyan-forming layer (drawn 495-740 nm), g = magenta-forming layer (the sheet draws it from 389 nm, starting at 0.0 with a near vertical stroke down to about -0.46 at 395 nm; traced from 395 nm), b = yellow-forming layer (379-510 nm).","Spectral dye density: process RA-4, diffuse spectral density, absolute (not normalised) with x axis 350-700 nm; curves are drawn from 380 nm; yellow peaks at about 450 nm (a shoulder near 420 nm), magenta at 550 nm, cyan at about 635 nm. All three start between 1.3 and 1.45 at 380 nm and the steep first 20 nm overlap; there is no minimum-density or neutral curve.","No grain data, D-min values or log H reference are printed in this sheet."]}